     RETURN False\n        self.users[username] = password\n        CALL self.save_users()\n        RETURN True\n\n    FUNCTION save_users() -> None\n        OPEN \'users.txt\' FOR writing\n        FOR EACH username, password IN self.users\n            WRITE username + \',\' + password + \'\\n\'\n        END FOR\n    END FUNCTION\nEND CLASS\n\n<form method="POST">\n    <label for="username">Username:</label>\n    <input type="text" name="username" required>\n    <label for="password">Password:</label>\n    <input type="password" name="password" required>\n    <input type="submit" value="Register">\n</form>\n```\n**Third-Party Libraries**:\n- **Flask:** Assists in web server functionality.\n\n---\n', '|Case|:**login**\n```pseudocode\nFUNCTION login()\n    IF METHOD IS POST\n        username = GET input from form with NAME \'username\'\n        password = GET input from form with NAME \'password\'\n\n        IF user_manager.login(username, password) IS TRUE\n            STORE username IN session\n            REDIRECT to /travel_details\n        ELSE\n            RETURN "Invalid credentials. Please try again."\n        ENDIF\n    ENDIF\n    RENDER login.html\nENDIF\n```\n**Key Functionality**: This function handles user login by verifying credentials and managing session state using Flask.\n\n---\n|Case|:**view_recommendations**\n```pseudocode\nFUNCTION travel_details()\n    IF METHOD IS POST\n        destination = GET input from form with NAME \'destination\'\n        duration = GET input from form with NAME \'duration\'\n        interests = GET selected input from form with NAME \'interests\'\n        \n        tips = tip_generator.generate_tips(destination, duration, interests)\n        RENDER travel_details.html WITH tips\n    ENDIF\n    RENDER travel_details.html WITH empty tips\nENDIF\n```\n**Key Functionality**: Collects travel details from user input, generates tips, and renders them in the template.\n\n---']
